    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "O'Mahony Walsh are delighted to present No. 4 Manor Hill to the market, a superb 3 bedroom, 1-bathroom detached bungalow. Ideally located within the highly sought-after Manor Hill development, just minutes' walk from Ballincollig Town Centre and all its amenities.\n\nThis inviting home enjoys a sunny, south-facing rear garden and an exceptional location, just minutes' walk from Ballincollig Town Centre, local amenities, convenient bus links and direct access to The Regional Park.\n\nRare opportunity to own a detached property in this quiet and private location less than 200 meters from the western link road\n\nHallway (5.80m x 2.82m)\nA bright and inviting entrance hallway with tiled flooring. Access to all accommodation.\n\nLiving Room (5.11m x 3.57m)\nA bright and spacious living room with an electric fire that can also be easily converted back to an open fireplace. A large front aspect window offers plenty of natural light. This is the perfect space to relax and spend time with family.\n\nOpen Plan Kitchen/Dining (7.18m x 4.69m)\nA fully fitted kitchen with integrated appliances including a Zanussi oven, hob and extractor fan, Norde Mende washing machine, Candy dryer, Sharp microwave, Indesit fridge freezer and a stainless-steel sink. Large side and rear aspect windows provide a flood of natural light.\n\nThe dining area is perfect for enjoying home cooked meals or entertaining guests with convenient rear access to the south facing garden.\n\nMaster Bedroom (3.97m x 3.54m)\nSpacious double bedroom with a large rear aspect window looking out into the south facing garden. Fitted wardrobes provide ample storage for your belongings.\n\nBedroom 2 (3.19m x 2.43m)\nDouble bedroom with fitted wardrobes and a side aspect window offers plenty of light.\n\nBedroom 3 (3.59m x 2.39m)\nDouble bedroom with a front aspect window, fitted wardrobes and units ideal for storage.\n\nFamily Bathroom (2.44m x 2.00m)\nFully tiled 3-piece suite with a Triton electric shower and a side aspect window. Access to attic.\n\nGarden Details\nTo the front, the property benefits from a concrete driveway providing off-street parking for two cars. The home is ideally positioned within a family-friendly estate and enjoys a great setting within walking distance of a bus stop.\n\nThe sun filled south-facing rear garden is mainly laid out to lawn and is fully enclosed with walled in boundaries, providing a safe and private outdoor space. A timber Barna shed offers excellent additional storage, while a pathway wraps around the property with gated side access to both sides. This garden is a great setting for al fresco dining, entertaining, or relaxing during the warmer months.\n\nHeating:\nGas Central Heating\n\nBER Details\nBER: E2 BER No: 113587463 Energy Performance Indicator: 354.95 kWh/m2/yr\n\n"
      },
